WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.480
We know how to shift a row.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.840
Now reverse the order in which
the cyclic positions are read.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:09.480
If h of X has coefficients h
zero through h n minus one,

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:13.240
define h star by replacing
X with X inverse.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:16.970
Since X inverse equals
X to the n minus one,

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:19.460
the result stays in the same group ring.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:22.640
The constant coefficient stays fixed.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.100
The remaining positions are read backward.

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.780
Use four generic coefficients
to see this clearly: a, b,

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.660
c, d becomes a, d, c, b.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.500
The coefficients keep their values;
only their cyclic positions reverse.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:44.040
Return to our original polynomial,

00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.560
negative one plus X plus
X squared plus X cubed.

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:54.100
Its star is negative one plus X inverse

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:58.890
plus X to the negative two
plus X to the negative three.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.740
Reduce exponents modulo four.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.460
The result is negative
one plus X cubed plus X

00:01:06.460 --> 00:01:10.360
squared plus X, which is
our original polynomial.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.500
This particular row is unchanged because
its final three coefficients are equal.

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:18.640
Why is star well defined?

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:23.760
The rule defining our group
ring is X to the n equals one.

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:27.400
Its inverse also has nth power one.

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:31.860
Replacing X by X inverse therefore
respects that defining relation,

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.680
so equal ring elements
still have equal stars.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:40.240
Reverse twice, and every position
returns to where it started.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.220
The star of h star is h.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.160
Replacing X by X inverse
also respects multiplication.

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:50.320
In this commutative group ring,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:54.540
the star of f times g
is f star times g star.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.500
Thus star is an involution of the ring.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:02.180
Remember what star does: it
reverses cyclic positions.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.600
It neither negates the coefficients nor
takes the reciprocal of the polynomial.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.140
We introduced it because multiplying
h by its reversal will encode

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:16.140
every cyclic dot product
in a single polynomial.
